// Flags `x as unknown as T` double-assertions. Biome has no built-in rule for this
// (noExplicitAny only catches `as any`), so this GritQL plugin fills the gap. Use a
// type guard, `satisfies`, or a typed fixture instead.
//
// Diagnostic-only BY DESIGN — do not add a `$cast => ...` rewrite. The obvious
// fix (`$value as $type`) is exactly the direct cast that TS2352 rejects (the
// double-assertion exists to silence it), so an autofix would either break the
// build or assert unsoundly. The real remediation needs human judgment.
`$value as unknown as $type` where {
  register_diagnostic(
    span = $value,
    message = "Avoid `as unknown as` double-assertions — use a type guard, `satisfies`, or a typed fixture."
  )
}
